Vauta's code uses Apple system frameworks, the system SQLite library and one
third-party package, a pinned fork of MLX (with its dependency swift-numerics),
which runs the optional search model and the optional integrated language model
(below). It bundles two third-party neural-network models (weights, not code)
for on-device speaker separation, described below. Two further models, the
optional search model and the optional integrated language model, are not
bundled: they are downloaded only when the user asks.

